{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.salesforce.mobilesdk.SalesforceSDKCore\/documentation\/SalesforceSDKCore","doc:\/\/com.salesforce.mobilesdk.SalesforceSDKCore\/documentation\/SalesforceSDKCore\/LoginHostListViewController"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Marks this host list as a standalone login screen rather than a sub-sheet of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"another login screen. This is the case in the forced-advanced-auth path, where"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the host list is the screen the user lands on and SFLoginViewController (which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"would otherwise own this chrome) is never created."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"presentedAsLoginScreen"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"set"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When set, this screen takes on the chrome that normally lives on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SFLoginViewController: the navigation-bar back button (shown when there is an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"account or flow to return to) and the dev-only gear \/ “Login Options” menu."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The two are gated independently — the back button by the account\/flow logic in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"-shouldShowBackButton, the gear by dev-support being enabled — this flag only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","te